  var rowFor, draw;
  ZS_SMART_PARTS.after(function () {
    rowFor = SEC.rowFor;
    draw = SEC.draw;
  });

  /* ══ the ready-made library ═══════════════════════════════════════
     Thirty-one starting points, in four families, and the order of those
     families is the product's order and not an accident: MOVEMENT AND ACCESS
     comes first because taking physical effort out of playing is what this
     box is for. Aim, firing and quality-of-life follow.

     Rules every entry here obeys:

       · the DESCRIPTION says what it FEELS like, never what it emits. "You
         can let go of the stick and keep running", not "holds ly+ for 8000 ms".
       · control names come from {tokens} (see fillNames), so a DualSense owner
         reads R2 and an Xbox owner reads RT without a second copy of the text.
       · every preset builds steps that pass the BOARD's validator — walked
         through profiles/schema.validate() and actions/steps.build_steps() by
         board/agent/tests/unit/test_preset_actions.py, at its defaults AND at
         both ends of every slider. A preset that cannot be expressed in the
         board's step vocabulary is not in this list.
       · nothing here needs a keyboard or a mouse. Every default trigger is a
         control on the pad, which is the whole reason Caleb's actions were
         dead: the app used to resolve "Fire" through the default profile's
         MOUSE binding. ONE DELIBERATE EXCEPTION (D280): Turn assist is a
         mouse accommodation by its nature, so it starts on keyboard X, and
         it is the one a mouse-and-keyboard config gets by default
         (ZS_SMART.seedTurnAssist, 21-rooms-exports.js).

     A note on the ones that tap the very control that starts them (rapid fire,
     bunny hop, hold-for-me): the board TAKES OVER that control for the length
     of the run — see actions/sequences.py set_takeover. Without that, your own
     finger holding the trigger merges with max() and the taps never reach the
     console, which is exactly what the shipped rapid fire used to do.

     shape of an entry:
       id     stable, for the colour and for tests
       fam    which family it files under
       ico    an icoSVG name (phone.html)
       n, d   name, and the plain-English description
       trig   the suggested trigger: {follow:'rt+'} follows whatever fires,
              {src:'BTN_TL'} is a literal control
       tunes  [] of sliders: {lab, val, min, max, step, unit, sub}
       pick   optional big three-way shortcut that writes tunes[into]
       btns   optional output buttons the user picks
       build(v, b, ctx) -> the action, with v the tune values in order,
              b the chosen buttons and ctx {ads: true|false|null} */

  var FAMILIES = [
    { k: 'aim', n: 'Aim', ico: 'target', col: '#58a6ff',
